<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eulmash-shakin-shumi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1004–988 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century-bce">10th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eulmash-shakin-shumi was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> from about 1004 to 988 BCE and founder of the short-lived Bazi Dynasty, which followed the Second <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sealand-dynasty">Sealand Dynasty</a>. He reigned for about seventeen years, the longest of the dynasty. Little is known of his reign beyond king lists and a few inscriptions.</p></div>
